---
description: Stop and notify the user if the persistent shell session becomes corrupted
alwaysApply: true
---

# Shell State Recovery

If the persistent shell session appears corrupted, stop immediately and tell the user so they can fix it.

- Treat errors like `cat: command not found`, `dump_bash_state: command not found`, or similar shell-wrapper failures as a broken persistent shell session.
- Do not continue trying workarounds in that session.
- Do not keep retrying unrelated commands.
- Tell the user the shell state appears broken and ask them to reload/reset it before continuing.
